        "note": "AutoDrift-style first-order/rate actuator filter is applied before Chrono driver inputs.",
        "status": "mapped_control_layer"
      },
      {
        "channel": "lf/lr/cg_shift/axle_load_split",
        "note": "Scenario carries lf/lr but current backend leaves Sedan geometry and load split unchanged.",
        "status": "not_mapped"
      },
      {
        "channel": "iz/inertia_scale",
        "note": "Scenario carries iz but current backend does not alter Chrono inertia tensors.",
        "status": "not_mapped"
      },
      {
        "channel": "cf/cr/tire_curve_family",
        "note": "Scenario carries cf/cr but current backend always uses Sedan TMeasy tire data.",
        "status": "not_mapped"
      },
      {
        "channel": "vehicle_model",
        "note": "The backend constructs veh.Sedan() unconditionally and the worker has no variant option.",
        "status": "not_mapped"
      }
    ],
    "hardcoded_sedan_constructor": true,
    "hardcoded_tmeasy_tire": true,
    "has_runtime_vehicle_variant_selector": false,
    "known_differences": [
      "vehicle model: Chrono Sedan (double wishbone / multilink, TMeasy tires, RWD, 4-speed automatic) vs AutoDrift single-track analytic model",
      "total mass matched by chassis-mass override; inertia, CG height/shift and per-axle load split remain the Sedan's, so iz / cg_shift / inertia_scale hidden parameters are NOT mapped",
      "tire stiffness scales (cf/cr) NOT mapped (TMeasy parameters fixed by the Sedan tire JSON); effective grip at a given mu differs from mu*g (measured ~1.1-1.25x at full braking)",
      "drive_scale / brake_scale mapped multiplicatively onto throttle/brake inputs and clipped at 1.0, so scales > 1.0 saturate",
      "max steering angle: Chrono Sedan 0.4363 rad at full lock vs AutoDrift max_steer 0.62 rad; the normalized steer command maps full-scale to full lock, so the physical steer gain is ~0.70x",
      "steer/drive first-order lags + steer rate limit replicated exactly at the 50 Hz control layer in front of the Chrono driver inputs; Chrono's own engine/transmission/brake dynamics act in addition (double shaping)",
      "initial state: pose and planar velocity (x, y, psi, vx, vy, yaw_rate) matched exactly at handoff after spin-up; suspension/driveline internal state is the spun-up straight-line state, not a curved steady state",
      "reset observation reports ax=ay=0 and zero actuator states (current-sim reports force-model accelerations at reset)",
      "ego acceleration channels are body-frame finite differences of vx/vy over the 0.02 s control step (current-sim uses instantaneous force-model accelerations)",
      "friction step changes terrain mu for the tires; AutoDrift additionally resamples speed_ref (reward-only, no actor/dynamics effect)",
      "AutoDrift aerodynamic drag/rolling resistance coefficients are not transferred; the Sedan's own drag and rolling resistance apply"
    ],
    "scenario_carries_lateral_params": true,
    "worker_constructs_default_backend": true,
    "worker_path": "scripts/feasibility_audit/chrono_backend_worker.py"
  },
  "decision": {
    "blocker": "The repository worker/backend still hard-code veh.Sedan() with TireModelType_TMEASY and expose no variant selector; scenario lf/lr/iz/cf/cr are carried but not mapped into Chrono dynamics.",
    "chrono_resource_summary": "Chrono data and Python wrappers contain multiple vehicle/tire resources.",
    "chrono_resources_support_extension": true,
    "direct_s4_hf_lite_pricing_admitted_now": false,
